        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0381" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg369"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.7962/64: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-17T15:00:00-00:44">March 17, 1942—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>83. From McBride. Department’s 53, March 13, 6 p.m. President Barclay assured me
                    today that fullest cooperation will be extended by Liberian health authorities.
                    United States forces will be given full control in defense areas and any
                    contiguous areas they may deem desirable. [McBride.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
